# Dark side of TDD and when should we use TDD
- TDD is Red - Green - Refactor
- Which is nothing but, we write failing test, write minimal code to pass and refactor.
  We keep doing it until we reach desired outcome.
- Dark Side
  1. Slower initial development.
      Writing tests before actual code takes time and in exploratory phases this feels like overhead.
      It may feel like building the guiderails before building the road.

  2. TDD has steep learning curve and need specific way of thinking to identify test cases, 
    now new developers may write poor quality tests or skip tests, this may lead to false confidence in delivery.


# Monolith vs Microservice ? When to use monolith architecture ? 
- In monolithic everything is in single application.
- Microserves seggregated into group of services.
- Microserves patterns are useful when we want to address scalability, fault tolerance and availability issues.
- Deploying specific services are easier which reduces down time for the end user.
- We can rely on event driven architecture to improve latency and throughput.
- For smaller applications with less number of users and less complexity we can go for monolithic.
- For exploratory POCs we can go with monolithic.

# Argument to use Microservice base architecture
- Timeline conflict. 
  How you will convince your product team that investing more time initially is better ?
    a. Here we will have to rely on non functional requirement like scalability, fault tolerance and availability.
    b. Product team have to agree on whether we want to match competetors metrics on availability and throughput,
        If no then it will be the product teams backlog in case users demand similar SLA.
    c. This will create technical debt for the team, later converting this into microservices will take time and product team will have to
        wait until microservices are ready to address the required SLA.
    d. With increased users, it will be difficult to manage the scale.
    e. It is better to invest time early to address these issues rather than creating technical debt for the team.
    f. If our competetors have solved these issues before us then they may take over the market share which we cannot afford.
    g. If we do not have any competetor in that case product team need to take call on whether they are okay with
        availability and throughput delivered by monolithic, it may lead to bad customer satisfaction if demands are high.
  


